Homepage: https://github.com/bceverly/restate
Description: serve restate repositories over HTTPS, append-only
 restate-proxy runs on the machine that stores restate repositories, and
 lets the machines that capture into them reach them over HTTPS without
 being able to remove or change what is there: a client may add a snapshot,
 and read, list and restore what its grant allows, and a capture cut off
 part way leaves nothing of itself behind.
 .
 Each client has a grant of its own in /etc/restate/proxy.d, naming its
 repository, what it may do and the hash of its token. Each connection is
 served by a process of its own, confined by Landlock and seccomp.
 .
 The package installs the restate-proxy service but neither enables nor
 starts it: it needs a certificate, its key and a grant first. See
 restate-proxy(8).

